
<h1>Performance overview</h1><p>A transparent delivery indicator for manager review.</p><form method="get" class="filter"><input type="hidden" name="page" value="reports"><label>Deadlines from<input type="date" name="from" value="<?=e($from)?>" required></label><label>To<input type="date" name="to" value="<?=e($to)?>" required></label><button>Apply</button><button name="csv" value="1" class="secondary">Export CSV</button></form>
<section class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Employee</th><th>Due tasks</th><th>Completed</th><th>On time</th><th>Score / 100</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($reports as $r): ?><tr><td><?=e($r['name'])?></td><td><?=e($r['total'])?></td><td><?=e($r['completed'])?></td><td><?=e($r['on_time'])?></td><td><?=e($r['score']??'N/A')?></td></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>How the score works</h2><p>Score = 60 × completed ÷ due tasks + 40 × on-time completions ÷ due tasks. Only deadlines in the selected range and before today count. Completions after the selected end date do not count. No eligible tasks means N/A.</p><p>This measures delivery, not work quality or task difficulty. Discuss blockers and workload before drawing conclusions. Reports use current task state; reopening a task changes its score, including earlier periods.</p></section>
